From: WelsonJS
Subject: [PATCH] ggml : move the I2_S reference (de)quantization to ggml-base

ggml.c (ggml-base) uses dequantize_row_i2_s (the I2_S type traits) and
quantize_i2_s (ggml_quantize_chunk), but the fork defines both in
ggml-cpu/quants.c, which is part of the CPU backend. That links in a static
build, and in shared builds on ELF platforms where undefined symbols are
resolved at load time. With GGML_BACKEND_DL on Windows each CPU variant is a
separate DLL that ggml-base.dll cannot link against, and the link fails with
LNK2001/LNK2019 for these two symbols.

Both functions are plain scalar C. Move them to ggml-quants.c and declare
them GGML_API, so the CPU backend (ops.cpp uses dequantize_row_i2_s) imports
them from ggml-base like the other reference quantization functions.

Apply with: git -c core.autocrlf=false apply <this file>

